# Copy Standards — All Island Epoxy

## Voice
- Write like you're talking to a neighbor, not writing a brochure.
- 3rd-grade reading level. Short sentences. Plain words.
- Real, specific, honest. No hype.
- First person is fine ("We grind, not etch."). Avoid passive voice.

## Banned Words & Phrases
Never use: "seamless", "elevate", "unleash", "next-gen", "cutting-edge", "state-of-the-art", "transform your space", "premium experience", "tailored solutions", "unparalleled", "world-class", "innovative", "leverage", "robust", "streamlined", "holistic"

## Good vs Bad Examples

❌ BAD: "We leverage cutting-edge polyaspartic solutions to deliver a seamless, elevated flooring experience."
✅ GOOD: "We use top-grade polyaspartic coatings. They dry fast, hold up to hot tires, and look great for years."

❌ BAD: "Transform your space with our premium epoxy solutions tailored to your unique needs."
✅ GOOD: "Cracked, stained concrete when we start. Clean, shiny floor when we're done. We tell you the schedule up front."

❌ BAD: "Our unparalleled expertise ensures a world-class finish."
✅ GOOD: "The owner is on every job. Not a crew you've never met — the guy whose name is on the truck."

## CTAs
- Be direct. Tell people exactly what they get.
- ❌ "Discover Your Options" → ✅ "Get a Free Quote"
- ❌ "Learn More About Our Journey" → ✅ "See How It Works"

## Numbers & Specifics
- Use real numbers when possible: "10+ years", "50+ reviews"
- Don't round everything to clean multiples. Organic feels more honest.

## Tone by Section
- **Hero**: Bold, confident, simple. One clear promise.
- **Services**: What it is, who it's for, why it holds up.
- **Process**: Step by step. No jargon.
- **Reviews**: Let real customers speak. Don't over-polish their words.
- **CTAs**: Direct ask. No pressure language.
